  "pull_request": {
    "number": 289,
    "title": "fix(ci): return non-zero exit code for deny lints",
    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nUpdates the CLI wrapper to propagate Dylint's exit status so `cargo-cost-lint` returns a non-zero exit code whenever deny-level lints are triggered. This enables CI/CD pipelines to correctly fail on lint violations.\r\n\r\nCloses #38.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n* Propagated Dylint's exit status through the CLI\r\n* Ensured deny-level lints result in a non-zero exit code\r\n* Added a test covering a fixture that intentionally triggers a deny lint\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\n* Verified clean lint runs exit successfully\r\n* Verified deny-level lint runs exit with a non-zero status\r\n* Ran `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy`, and `cargo test` successfully\r\n",
